# Check every file out exactly as committed, on every platform.
#
# WHY REPO-WIDE, and not a list of globs: the third-party-notices staleness
# gate (`prebuild:electron`) hashes file BYTES and compares them to values
# recorded in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Git's default `text=auto` rewrites LF to
# CRLF on a Windows checkout, so any hashed text file comes out with different
# bytes and the gate fails against files nobody edited.
#
# That gate hashes two separate sets — package-lock.json, and every vendored
# font PLUS its license file (`computeVendoredHash`). The first attempt at this
# fix pinned only package-lock.json; the very next Windows build then failed on
# `public/fonts/**/*.txt` instead. Enumerating the hashed inputs is a list that
# goes stale the moment someone adds a font or hashes another file, and it goes
# stale silently — on a platform nobody develops on.
#
# So: no EOL conversion, anywhere. Verified 2026-08-21 — the committed LF
# package-lock.json hashes to the recorded value, the CRLF version does not.
* -text
